name 'building-data-driven-systems-postassessment-q3_2025'

question 'A team is designing a schema for a "Task Manager" app. They decide each task must have a `title` (string), `priority` (number), and `isCompleted` (boolean). Why is defining these data types important before writing the code?'

wrong 'It ensures that the AI will write the CSS styling correctly.'
wrong 'It prevents the app from needing a database.'
right 'It allows the team to predict how data will be rendered and ensures the AI scaffold generates valid logic for those types.'
wrong 'It makes the website load faster on older browsers.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 2

Establishing a schema before coding ensures that the interface (rendering) and the logic (functions) are aligned. If the code expects a number but receives a string, the app will likely fail. 
MARKDOWN
